WEBVTT

00:12.420 --> 00:13.730
Whoa...

00:13.730 --> 00:15.030
What's so surprising?

00:16.000 --> 00:20.040
We knew from sighting reports 
that it was in this area.

00:20.040 --> 00:21.450
Investigate it at once.

00:21.850 --> 00:26.380
Now? In the dark? We won't find anything!

00:26.380 --> 00:29.630
I didn't ask for your opinion. Get to it.

00:31.370 --> 00:32.790
Understood...

00:32.790 --> 00:37.060
But, Kiggith, 
what are you so wary of?

00:37.060 --> 00:39.560
You even had us abandon the 
hideout we arranged for you.

00:40.520 --> 00:43.310
Do you not hear the footsteps?

00:48.960 --> 00:53.030
Approaching silently, it's ready to pounce

00:53.600 --> 00:55.280
with its fangs bared.

00:56.030 --> 00:57.900
They're the footsteps of a spider.

00:59.700 --> 01:03.540
<b>The Daily Life of
the Former Hero and the Assassin</b>

01:12.380 --> 01:15.110
<i>I go to sleep at night and 
wake up in the morning.</i>

01:15.600 --> 01:17.460
<i>It's one of the small joys in life.</i>

01:46.470 --> 01:48.920
Morning stretches complete.

01:49.600 --> 01:50.880
<i>The brightness of the morning sun.</i>

01:52.000 --> 01:53.790
<i>The pleasure of exercise.</i>

01:54.240 --> 01:56.470
<i>The spotlessness of a 
place freshly cleaned...</i>

01:57.120 --> 02:00.760
<i>These were all things I had once cast aside, 
deeming them unnecessary for a hero.</i>

02:01.600 --> 02:06.560
<i>But I get to experience them thanks to
 "New Truth," the new Blessing created within me.</i>

02:07.490 --> 02:11.180
<i>Almighty Demis didn't 
bestow me with New Truth.</i>

02:12.170 --> 02:16.490
<i>It's less a blessing and more 
a power born of my free will.</i>

02:16.830 --> 02:18.380
<i>At least, that's what I believe.</i>

02:19.640 --> 02:21.450
Now this is the slow life.

02:22.100 --> 02:23.870
Morning, Mr. Crawly Wawly.

02:41.020 --> 02:44.290
The herb farm is starting to come together.

02:44.290 --> 02:44.680
Yep.

02:45.270 --> 02:47.990
But I couldn't have done 
it without you, Tisse.

02:47.990 --> 02:51.380
I have no experience growing herbs,

02:51.380 --> 02:53.820
so I'm not sure I'm actually being useful.

02:53.820 --> 02:55.820
Two heads are better than one.

02:59.870 --> 03:06.080
I really didn't expect you 
to propose this, though.

03:07.440 --> 03:09.170
Adventuring is my side gig.

03:09.170 --> 03:11.580
Growing herbs will be my main job.

03:11.940 --> 03:16.090
Are you doing this to help Red?

03:16.400 --> 03:18.060
That's a big part of it.

03:18.460 --> 03:24.350
But mostly, I just wanted to do something 
that didn't involve my battle prowess.

03:25.560 --> 03:26.850
That's wonderful.

03:27.400 --> 03:28.530
About last night—

03:28.530 --> 03:30.850
Well, let's get to work.

03:32.410 --> 03:33.540
Miss Ruti!

03:37.190 --> 03:39.030
Can you tell what's wrong, Mr. Crawly Wawly?

03:42.550 --> 03:45.150
The soil is stone cold, apparently.

03:45.150 --> 03:47.530
It's true. But why?

03:48.000 --> 03:50.990
We lack the knowledge to fix this.

03:50.990 --> 03:53.040
We should ask Red to take a look.

03:54.750 --> 03:57.830
Looks like the growth of 
cold mold is the cause.

03:57.830 --> 04:01.050
Cold mold? Like the stuff 
that grows in caves?

04:01.430 --> 04:02.460
Yeah.

04:02.460 --> 04:04.910
It absorbs heat from everything close by.

04:05.340 --> 04:09.060
Only the huge colonies can 
cause problems to adventurers,

04:09.060 --> 04:12.770
but on farms, even trace 
amounts can cause disease.

04:13.470 --> 04:16.680
These issues are part and parcel 
of starting a farm, unfortunately.

04:16.680 --> 04:17.480
Right.

04:18.440 --> 04:22.600
But because you noticed it 
and came to me immediately,

04:22.600 --> 04:24.270
we may be able to fix this.

04:25.320 --> 04:26.450
Will you help me out?

04:26.900 --> 04:29.700
Of course. This is my herb farm.

05:01.790 --> 05:02.940
All done. Great job.

05:03.520 --> 05:06.490
If the chemicals we sprayed 
get rid of the cold mold,

05:06.490 --> 05:08.850
the herbs should recover in time.

05:08.850 --> 05:09.700
Good.

05:10.480 --> 05:13.460
Let's show some faith in your herbs.

05:13.460 --> 05:16.530
Right. Thank you, Big Brother.

05:16.530 --> 05:17.120
Sure.

05:18.640 --> 05:20.710
Miss Ruti has changed.

05:21.090 --> 05:26.190
She sure has. Look how hard she's 
trying to save these young herbs.

05:27.500 --> 05:30.220
You never could've seen her like 
this back when she was the Hero.

05:30.780 --> 05:33.720
This is her ideal vision of a slow life.

05:36.880 --> 05:38.330
But I...

05:48.610 --> 05:50.620
<i>The two of them will be fine.</i>

05:52.450 --> 05:53.870
<i>I'm Tisse.</i>

05:54.480 --> 05:56.550
<i>A member of the Assassins' Guild,</i>

05:56.550 --> 05:59.870
<i>and an assassin with nefarious 
plans to oversleep this morning.</i>

06:04.260 --> 06:06.780
G-Good morning.

06:06.780 --> 06:07.900
Morning.

06:07.900 --> 06:09.190
What are your plans for the day?

06:09.190 --> 06:11.550
Tending to the herbs.

06:11.550 --> 06:14.460
I took care of that already. What else?

06:17.570 --> 06:19.140
Nothing in particular.

06:20.600 --> 06:24.650
Good. I want you to accompany me today.

06:25.760 --> 06:27.150
For what?

06:28.110 --> 06:30.160
A very important task.

06:33.630 --> 06:37.410
<i>Huh? Why are we having 
breakfast like always?</i>

06:43.940 --> 06:46.420
<i>And why are we taking a bath now?</i>

06:47.510 --> 06:48.480
Tisse...

06:51.120 --> 06:52.930
Y-Yes?

06:53.460 --> 06:54.830
You like baths.

07:03.650 --> 07:04.440
E-

07:04.700 --> 07:07.440
Enough to write my own review book, yes.

07:08.130 --> 07:11.450
Big Brother's cooking is 
the best in the world.

07:12.140 --> 07:13.950
It is very delicious, yes.

07:15.240 --> 07:16.450
So you get it.

07:16.760 --> 07:18.100
<i>Get what?!</i>

07:19.720 --> 07:21.520
Hook, line, and sinker.

07:24.530 --> 07:26.460
<i>Something's going down, 
and I don't know what!</i>

07:32.520 --> 07:34.680
<i>I wonder what this very important task is.</i>

07:35.190 --> 07:38.880
Big Brother bought me a hairpin here.

07:38.880 --> 07:41.190
It's very nice.

07:41.190 --> 07:41.770
Yep.

07:46.100 --> 07:50.780
<i>Is she telling me this is a crime 
scene and to stay on my toes?!</i>

07:51.200 --> 07:53.030
I'll keep my eyes peeled.

07:54.300 --> 07:54.970
Good.

07:57.020 --> 07:58.000
Eek!

07:58.780 --> 08:00.450
A drake's running wild!

08:04.760 --> 08:06.160
I'll stop it.

08:06.160 --> 08:08.320
No. I'll handle it.

08:08.940 --> 08:10.590
But it might become a big mess...

08:13.180 --> 08:14.050
Sit.

08:17.010 --> 08:18.820
That thing's sent many a trainer

08:18.820 --> 08:21.480
to the hospital, and she made it sit!

08:18.820 --> 08:21.480
Look, that unruly beast is 
acting like a house cat!

08:21.820 --> 08:24.150
Yeah, I knew she'd draw attention.

08:28.840 --> 08:30.670
The scenery here is very pretty.

08:31.110 --> 08:33.690
And there's always a 
pleasant breeze blowing by.

08:33.690 --> 08:35.320
Is that so?

08:36.180 --> 08:38.830
<i>So, is this where the important task is?</i>

08:42.400 --> 08:43.590
Miss Ruti?

08:45.700 --> 08:46.790
You there.

08:48.100 --> 08:50.640
There's a monster lying dormant underground.

08:50.640 --> 08:52.020
It needs to be dealt with.

08:52.020 --> 08:54.130
Huh? Where did that come from?

08:54.550 --> 08:57.180
Don't say I didn't warn you.

09:06.520 --> 09:07.730
A man-eating earthworm!

09:07.730 --> 09:11.360
It attacks and devours any people it finds
 when it awakens from hibernation!

09:12.250 --> 09:13.280
Hi-yah.

09:19.390 --> 09:21.080
Holy cow!

09:21.080 --> 09:25.250
Would you happen to be Zoltan's 
strongest adventurer, Miss Ruti?!

09:25.660 --> 09:28.010
Anybody could've executed that chop.

09:28.010 --> 09:30.510
I'm a perfectly run-of-the-mill adventurer.

09:30.510 --> 09:33.760
Splitting a man-eating earthworm in two 
with your bare hands won't go unnoticed.

09:39.830 --> 09:41.810
<i>Now we're at the theater.</i>

09:41.810 --> 09:44.020
<i>What happened to the task?</i>

09:44.320 --> 09:47.350
The lead's acting in this 
play is the talk of the town.

09:47.350 --> 09:48.830
I'm sure it'll be fun.

09:48.830 --> 09:53.530
It's the story of a knight and a 
bandit falling for the same woman.

09:53.970 --> 09:57.900
Stop it, you two! 
We all go way back, don't we?

09:58.360 --> 10:00.310
What a tense development.

10:00.840 --> 10:01.430
Huh?

10:07.210 --> 10:09.180
That sword has been cursed.

10:09.180 --> 10:10.960
You should throw it away at once.

10:11.250 --> 10:13.360
Don't give me that!

10:13.360 --> 10:17.680
My acting has improved so much 
since I got my hands on this thing!

10:17.680 --> 10:20.970
Like hell I'm just gonna throw it all away!

10:23.560 --> 10:25.130
A devil of arts.

10:25.130 --> 10:28.940
They possess people and bestow them with 
talent in exchange for their lifespan.

10:34.120 --> 10:37.690
I'm just your friendly neighborhood 
adventurer. Very ordinary.

10:38.150 --> 10:43.700
Wow! Who could've ever expected that the 
two were fighting because of a devil?!

10:45.500 --> 10:47.450
The play isn't over yet!

10:47.450 --> 10:49.010
Use this!

10:50.760 --> 10:56.130
Adventurer! Please save the person I love!

11:05.480 --> 11:08.270
She's drawing attention like never before.

11:08.270 --> 11:11.570
The audience will probably never 
forget this for as long as they live.

11:21.290 --> 11:23.550
You gave out a bunch of autographs.

11:23.550 --> 11:25.580
I wasn't trying to draw attention.

11:25.580 --> 11:30.210
I hear the play's switching to a screenplay 
featuring the Adventurer Ruti tomorrow.

11:31.920 --> 11:32.890
Oh...

11:32.890 --> 11:34.030
Here you are!

11:35.070 --> 11:39.350
You're well known as a Zoltan adventurer now.

11:39.350 --> 11:41.260
I don't think it's anything to worry about.

11:41.610 --> 11:44.510
But today was important.

11:45.260 --> 11:48.550
What were you even trying to do today?

11:51.990 --> 11:54.730
<i>Huh? Miss Ruti's feeling down for once.</i>

11:55.010 --> 11:58.130
The day's not done yet. 
There's time to turn things around.

11:58.130 --> 11:59.380
Can we?

11:59.380 --> 12:00.000
Yeah.

12:04.410 --> 12:06.030
So, how are things lately?

12:21.140 --> 12:23.380
Anything bothering you?

12:23.380 --> 12:29.380
Er... I'm a little concerned about how 
strange you've been acting today.

12:30.970 --> 12:32.520
Nothing ever goes right.

12:32.520 --> 12:35.260
Um, what's the matter?

12:37.800 --> 12:41.230
It seemed like you've been
 worried about something lately,

12:41.230 --> 12:43.780
so I planned today to help
 take your mind off things.

12:44.720 --> 12:49.970
And then, I was going to treat you to 
your favorite oden and hear you vent.

12:50.510 --> 12:52.410
Is that so...

12:52.410 --> 12:55.820
Yep. But it didn't go too well...

12:56.830 --> 12:57.930
I think.

12:58.340 --> 13:03.300
<i>She's so strong that today's events 
all felt inconsequential to her.</i>

13:03.990 --> 13:06.730
<i>So she never even considered that 
they would cause such a scene.</i>

13:07.340 --> 13:09.140
<i>She really is abnormal.</i>

13:09.870 --> 13:10.310
<i>But...</i>

13:12.070 --> 13:14.060
You're too kind.

13:14.060 --> 13:16.200
I keep messing things up.

13:16.200 --> 13:18.260
You're always having to clean up after me.

13:18.260 --> 13:20.560
Has that been bothering you?

13:23.380 --> 13:27.490
I did my best to keep a low profile 
by not using any special skills.

13:27.490 --> 13:29.650
I also kept insisting that 
I was an ordinary adventurer.

13:29.650 --> 13:31.900
I get the feeling it had the opposite effect.

13:33.080 --> 13:34.080
Oh...

13:34.080 --> 13:37.200
But you're a lot better off than before.

13:37.200 --> 13:39.600
You thought I was even worse than this?

13:41.890 --> 13:45.590
I tore my hair out when you threw 
that knight off the bridge.

13:45.590 --> 13:46.470
Grr.

13:49.930 --> 13:52.380
<i>Thank you very much, Miss Ruti.</i>

13:53.080 --> 13:54.660
<i>No need to worry about me.</i>

13:55.370 --> 13:58.060
<i>It'll all be over by morning.</i>

14:03.790 --> 14:05.490
What are you doing?

14:06.040 --> 14:09.490
We've finished investigating the airship, 
so we're writing up a report.

14:13.190 --> 14:16.500
Leave out any and all information 
about Tisse. Delete this.

14:16.500 --> 14:19.260
No can do.

14:19.260 --> 14:25.960
Her being here means that there's a possibility
 the airship belongs to the Hero Ruti.

14:26.840 --> 14:28.920
Leaving out such critical information

14:28.920 --> 14:31.140
would constitute an act of 
treachery against Cardinal Ljubo.

14:36.950 --> 14:39.480
I can't have you reporting this.

14:39.810 --> 14:44.980
Settling the score with Tisse is far more 
important to me than the Church's orders.

14:53.410 --> 14:55.420
I can't wait...

14:55.420 --> 14:56.750
My archenemy.

15:13.010 --> 15:14.530
It's been a while,

15:15.040 --> 15:16.600
Kiggith Viper.

15:16.880 --> 15:22.880
It brings back memories of our days training 
under our master when I see you like this,

15:22.880 --> 15:24.610
Tisse Garland.

15:24.870 --> 15:29.990
The Assassins' Guild has only one 
way of dealing with deserters.

15:30.730 --> 15:32.610
I trust you're fully aware of that.

15:33.780 --> 15:35.650
I like the bloodlust in your eyes.

15:35.650 --> 15:39.060
No wonder our master saw 
great potential in you.

15:39.060 --> 15:41.870
Which means killing you here 
would be a crying shame.

15:42.180 --> 15:43.530
What are you implying?

15:43.530 --> 15:46.510
Why don't you join me?

15:47.020 --> 15:49.880
You have what it takes 
to be my right-hand man.

15:50.910 --> 15:53.130
What happened to your allies?

15:53.130 --> 15:54.610
I killed them.

15:54.610 --> 15:58.390
They were about to get in the way of 
my battle with you, my greatest prey.

15:58.710 --> 16:02.600
Then I have no qualms about killing you.

16:02.600 --> 16:05.150
The Guild does not take betrayal lightly.

16:05.150 --> 16:09.900
That's just it. You're sorely lacking 
in an assassin's thirst for murder.

16:11.900 --> 16:13.460
As your fellow student and mentor,

16:13.460 --> 16:16.740
I'll teach you what it 
truly means to be an assassin.

16:43.340 --> 16:45.240
You're better than I remember.

16:45.240 --> 16:47.060
But how will you deal with these?

16:57.220 --> 17:02.000
What now? If you dodge them, 
this airship will be destroyed.

17:02.260 --> 17:05.360
Aren't you here for the airship?

17:05.360 --> 17:08.230
Besides, that skill kills 
innocent bystanders, too.

17:08.230 --> 17:10.250
That's why Master forbade 
us from ever using it.

17:10.560 --> 17:13.320
That's why I said you're lacking in thirst.

17:13.320 --> 17:15.140
We have our Blessings and our skills.

17:15.140 --> 17:18.950
All an assassin needs to do 
is fight as they will us to.

17:18.950 --> 17:22.470
That realization is why
 I left the Assassins' Guild!

17:33.400 --> 17:38.640
<i>Kiggith used to be more faithful to 
his Assassin's Blessing than I was.</i>

17:40.710 --> 17:43.130
<i>So why did he end up like this?</i>

17:44.790 --> 17:45.790
Got you!

17:57.280 --> 17:58.560
It's over.

17:58.560 --> 18:00.680
Any last words?

18:01.180 --> 18:03.680
D-Don't kill me.

18:04.180 --> 18:07.920
I'm in the employ of 
Cardinal Ljubo of the Church.

18:08.470 --> 18:10.440
Don't you want to know more?

18:13.580 --> 18:16.190
How could you reveal your client's name?

18:16.440 --> 18:20.400
I'll tell you everything I know.

18:20.400 --> 18:22.860
So spare my life...

18:23.340 --> 18:26.250
Ljubo wants the airship.

18:26.250 --> 18:27.710
<i>He refuses to uphold</i>

18:26.250 --> 18:29.020
He plans to have it airborne

18:27.710 --> 18:30.590
<i>even the most fundamental 
rules of being an assassin.</i>

18:29.020 --> 18:31.200
as soon as possible.

18:31.200 --> 18:35.460
<i>The man I see before me is 
simply a disgraceful murderer!</i>

18:47.850 --> 18:51.400
<i>Kiggith could only adhere to his Blessing.</i>

18:52.080 --> 18:54.150
<i>He had no will of his own.</i>

19:01.510 --> 19:02.770
Miss Ruti.

19:04.020 --> 19:05.230
Is it over?

19:05.230 --> 19:10.370
Yes. He was a rogue assassin who 
deserted the Assassins' Guild.

19:10.370 --> 19:11.170
I see.

19:12.300 --> 19:17.460
The Guild isn't as authoritarian 
as people seem to think it is.

19:18.150 --> 19:21.210
You're allowed to turn down 
missions you don't want to take.

19:21.210 --> 19:23.100
You're even free to retire.

19:23.740 --> 19:27.970
Our Blessings have fated us to live 
as assassins, so we need a place

19:27.970 --> 19:30.100
where we can help each other live.

19:30.100 --> 19:34.150
That place, and that organization, 
is the Assassins' Guild.

19:34.400 --> 19:38.100
Surprising. 
Everyone thinks it's a scary place.

19:38.100 --> 19:40.040
That's our marketing strategy.

19:40.040 --> 19:43.560
Even the rule about not accepting 
unreasonable missions was established

19:43.560 --> 19:48.060
so we would have just cause and 
not be wiped out by higher powers.

19:48.060 --> 19:51.120
We're all just doing everything 
we can to survive.

19:53.610 --> 19:56.090
So you're not allowed to 
murder without reason?

19:56.320 --> 20:00.680
Exactly. Carrying out assassinations 
left and right would be problematic.

20:04.940 --> 20:07.270
But they are still assassinations 
at the end of the day.

20:07.270 --> 20:10.850
And I made you, the Hero, help with one.

20:11.250 --> 20:13.850
Is that why you wouldn't talk to me about it?

20:13.850 --> 20:17.860
Your desire is to live a 
slow life here in Zoltan...

20:17.860 --> 20:18.860
But I...

20:22.270 --> 20:26.560
I cannot quit being an assassin.

20:27.890 --> 20:32.370
So how would it be okay for 
me to stay by your side?

20:35.110 --> 20:38.950
Assassin or not, you're my friend.

20:39.500 --> 20:42.380
So you don't have to force 
yourself to change for me.

20:43.250 --> 20:45.890
You can just be a slow-life assassin instead.

20:47.310 --> 20:49.610
A slow-life assassin?

20:50.900 --> 20:51.630
What...

20:55.360 --> 20:57.150
What the heck is that supposed to mean?

20:57.430 --> 21:00.940
I'll continue to offer a helping 
hand whenever you need it.

21:01.420 --> 21:03.900
It doesn't matter that 
we're Hero and Assassin.

21:03.900 --> 21:05.150
I'll do it because I want to.

21:06.080 --> 21:07.470
Miss Ruti...

21:12.110 --> 21:15.810
So, please, talk to me next time.

21:15.810 --> 21:20.060
Yes... I will, Miss Ruti!

21:31.120 --> 21:33.680
This is unusually shoddy work for Kiggith.

21:34.160 --> 21:37.120
This doesn't even tell me 
where the airship is.

21:37.120 --> 21:39.110
I'll need him to lead me there in person.

21:41.700 --> 21:44.940
But this at least confirms 
the airship's existence.

21:45.580 --> 21:47.180
Summon Van back.

21:47.180 --> 21:48.580
Understood.

21:48.580 --> 21:51.920
No, wait. On second thought, I'll go.

21:51.920 --> 21:53.810
Is there any need for you to go personally?

21:53.810 --> 21:56.960
Once I meet up with Van, we'll head 
for Zoltan directly from there.

21:58.080 --> 22:03.490
<i>At last, it is time for my lofty 
ambitions to be realized.</i>

22:14.250 --> 22:18.480
<i>The Church's warriors can no longer 
keep up with the way Van fights.</i>

22:20.480 --> 22:23.230
Our party is in shambles. We should descend.

22:24.040 --> 22:26.400
But I can keep fighting.

22:26.820 --> 22:29.390
Maybe you can, but our party can't.

22:29.390 --> 22:31.130
Is that a problem?

22:31.130 --> 22:31.910
What?

22:32.290 --> 22:35.020
Only the Hero may save the world.

22:35.020 --> 22:38.540
Then any sacrifices made to 
develop the Hero's Blessing

22:38.540 --> 22:40.670
can be seen as justified 
for the sake of the world.

22:40.670 --> 22:41.840
No, they can't.

22:41.840 --> 22:44.420
Sighting the flare ordering 
us to descend the mountain!

22:48.280 --> 22:49.870
Cardinal Ljubo's orders?

22:49.870 --> 22:53.680
I'm glad. Finally my real 
adventure can begin.

22:54.050 --> 22:57.790
Do you have nothing to 
say to our dead comrades?

22:58.230 --> 22:59.690
The Hero need not look back.

23:00.270 --> 23:01.860
It's the phrase I like most

23:01.860 --> 23:03.800
from the texts on the 
Heroes across history.

